### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:3000/

### 2. Ingest Drug Interaction (Aspirin interacts with Warfarin)
POST http://localhost:3000/ingest/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "drug_a": "Aspirin",
    "drug_b": "Warfarin",
    "severity": "High"
}

### 3. Ingest Another Interaction (Ibuprofen interacts with Aspirin)
POST http://localhost:3000/ingest/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "drug_a": "Ibuprofen",
    "drug_b": "Aspirin",
    "severity": "Moderate"
}

### 4. Add Patient Medication (John Doe takes Aspirin)
POST http://localhost:3000/patient/add_medication
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": "john_doe",
    "drug": "Aspirin"
}

### 5. Add Patient Medication (John Doe takes Warfarin) -> Creates Risk!
POST http://localhost:3000/patient/add_medication
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": "john_doe",
    "drug": "Warfarin"
}

### 6. Check Risks for John Doe
# Expected: Should find the interaction between Aspirin and Warfarin
GET http://localhost:3000/patient/check_risks/john_doe

### 7. Infer Risks (Trigger Transformation)
# This runs the logic to infer new interactions based on chemical similarity 
# (Note: Requires 'chemically_similar' data to be present to show results, but endpoint will run)
POST http://localhost:3000/infer/risks
